     "result_text_tail": "that actually churned in 2026.\n\n**Numbers:** there are 150 in total. 56 are copied from the briefing pack with excerpts, and 94 are calculated, each with a live formula in the workbook. None are left as \"?\". None have a second, independent source, because the pack is the only one.\n\n**Choices I made in your place**\n- **Format:** a deep, 45-slide deck worked through as an issue tree, because this is a CEO launch decision.\n- **Success criteria:** reach 105% NRR by 2028, keep gross margin at or above 75%, and let the mobile rewrite slip by no more than two quarters.\n- **Out of scope:** changing the Core price, adding engineers, building an in-house AI model.\n- **Look:** the navy theme.\n- **Allowance:** about 667 AI requests per seat a month, set so inference uses at most half of the $12 premium. This is my design assumption, not from the pack.\n- **Pro usage:** Pro accounts are assumed to use Copilot at the beta average (3,600 requests a month).\n- **Run cost:** the $0.6M a year is counted as cost of revenue.\n\n**Limits:** the pack has no dispatcher wage data, so the time saved isn't priced in dollars. No Pro price other than $12 was tested; the Q1 test is meant to close that gap.\n\nI can switch the theme, cut the deck to about 30 slides, or rerun the numbers with different assumptions (Pro take-up, usage or allowance level).\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- brightwork-copilot.pptx\n- brightwork-copilot-sources.xlsx\n- brightwork-copilot.json (the editable source the deck is built from)"
